-- title:
--   Closedness of the Radon–Nikodym density graph
-- statement:
--   Let a commutative metric topological group $K$ act continuously on a Polish space $Z$, and let $M$ be a Borel probability measure on $Z$. Let $H$ consist of those $k\in K$ for which $k_*M$ and $M$ have the same null sets. Then
--   $$\left\{\left(k,\sqrt{d(k_*M)/dM}\right):k\in H\right\}$$
--   is closed in $K\times L^2(M;\mathbb R)$. This realizes the quasi-invariance subgroup as a closed density graph.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration MeasureEquivalenceRNGraph.isClosed_graph in RNGraph.lean, lines 129–145; local source SHA-256 cc8db11a6a4107f7ae6cf4e29673db3d07f1805fcbb02b5944b7deccfb1ca590. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

